    {
      "id": "h-diff",
      "text": "DIFFERENCE is XOR",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "p-diff",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "The difference bit behaves as the sum bit did. It is 1 exactly when the inputs differ, so DIFF = A XOR B, the same gate the adder used."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "h-borrow",
      "text": "BORROW needs an inverter",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "p-borrow",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Borrowing is different. You borrow only when taking 1 from 0, so BORROW = (NOT A) AND B, and that inverter is the one asymmetry with the half adder."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "h-compare",
